WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:07.250
Today, Michael Kinch, who is associate vice
chancellor at Washington University in St.

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:12.459
Louis and also author of Between Hope and
Fear, which is a History of Vaccines.

00:00:12.459 --> 00:00:13.750
So great to have you on today.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:18.590
Thanks for the opportunity so we could start
in so many different places, but let's just

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:23.710
maybe start with something that's a big topic
of discussion right now.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:28.070
We've seen sort of different numbers stated
about what the goal should be in terms of

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:31.349
the percentage of Americans or of global citizens.

00:00:31.349 --> 00:00:35.829
But maybe we'll start with Americans that
need to be vaccinated in order for the U.S.

00:00:35.829 --> 00:00:38.370
to approximate what would be called herd immunity.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:42.450
And, of course, there's a number of input
factors that determine what this number should

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:49.800
be, how contagious something is, how effective
the vaccines are, and all of these other things.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:53.199
What's what are the sort of the most important
things we should be thinking about now in

00:00:53.199 --> 00:00:58.859
terms of the variance, in terms of vaccine
hesitancy, all of these different input factors

00:00:58.859 --> 00:01:04.439
for if there is this this one number that
we should be looking at as as the sort of

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:06.060
threshold.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:13.380
Yes, and herd immunity is a term that it's
actually been misidentified and misused, particularly

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:17.400
by the previous administration, in a nutshell,
it's the likelihood that if you're someone

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:21.770
who is susceptible, let's say you were a cancer
patient who had chemotherapy to knock down

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:27.000
your immune system, what is the likelihood
that you will encounter someone in your vicinity

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.830
that might affect you?

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:34.360
And that number for sars-cov-2, the current
source of the pandemic has been creeping upwards.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.619
It started at about 70 percent.

00:01:36.619 --> 00:01:42.610
And it looks like today it's probably between
80 and 85 percent, in part because these new

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:46.560
variants, the British variant of the South
African variant, not to mention the Brazilian

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:51.180
variant that hasn't gotten as much press,
are far more communicative.

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:54.270
So I think we need to be shooting for eighty
five percent.

00:01:54.270 --> 00:02:00.360
And from a realistic standpoint, that means
that we need to have probably 90 to 95 percent

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:06.619
of the population protected because again,
some people will have had cancer therapy,

00:02:06.619 --> 00:02:08.580
rheumatoid arthritis treatment.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:12.090
There are simply old, very old or very young.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:16.190
And they may be immunized, but the immunization
may not take.

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:20.550
And so we're going to have to go in excess
of that 80 to 85 percent number in order to

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:23.430
assure that we finally get this virus behind
us.

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:30.980
Now, this this may be a silly question, but
I've not heard it addressed head on necessarily.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:35.030
When we talk about these numbers, I presume
we're talking about the entire population.

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:39.860
If you are not including people below a certain
age, at least initially, don't we really need

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:41.830
one hundred percent of eligible adults?

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:46.370
Because there are so many people under 18
or 16, which are the ages that the Fizer and

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:49.130
Moderna vaccines respectively have been tested
on?

00:02:49.130 --> 00:02:53.110
Don't we really need every adult vaccinated?

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:58.620
We do and essentially, again, that eighty
five percent number alone means that we need

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:04.360
that the vaccines are being tested in pediatric
populations, but we don't have the data yet.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:05.360
Right.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:08.870
And so every adult, in order to protect your
children and your grandchildren really needs

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:10.390
to be vaccinated soon.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:15.390
And as you mentioned, it's not just here in
the US, it's around the world, because when

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:22.520
you look at it, as we've seen, we have variants
coming out of South Africa and other countries.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:27.440
And that means that someone in one country
or a population of one country that decides

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:31.090
not to be vaccinated could actually jeopardize
the rest of the planet.

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:37.750
On on today's program, one of the things we
looked at was a new study that looked at the

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:41.370
current level of vaccine hesitancy in the
American population.

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:48.780
The good topline news is that the 60 65 percent
hesitancy of May 20 20 has been reduced dramatically.

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:53.900
It's now down, according to this latest study,
about a third of the country.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:59.610
When you slice and dice different groups,
three groups that are particularly or disproportionately

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:07.940
vaccine hesitant when it comes to this vaccination
are among political lines, Republicans among

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:13.760
racial lines, black Americans and among educational
lines, those without a college degree for

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:15.120
different reasons.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:19.120
These three groups seem to be hesitant of
the vaccine for different reasons.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:23.640
What historically have been some of the most
effective ways to get more buy in to mass

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:25.380
vaccination campaigns?

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:28.350
There are two things.

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:35.470
One is that we need to be 100 percent transparent,
both in what we know and what we don't know.

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:36.720
We're not here to sell a used car.

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:38.960
We're here to get past the pandemic.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:43.400
And so I think that we need to convey when
there is information that we don't know about,

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:44.410
we need to convey that.

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:48.460
But we also need to convey what we do know
and we need to stop rumors.

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:53.510
There have been rumors that are completely
unsubstantiated about causing lack of female

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:57.680
fertility or lack of male fertility and many
other things.

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:01.570
But we also need to respect that there are
certain populations of people, for example,

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:05.910
black Americans that were subjected, for example,
to the Tuskegee experiments.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:06.910
Right.

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:11.940
And that means that they're hesitant about
many different standardized medical procedures.

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:16.220
And we need to then explain to them, here
is what we know about it and why you're not

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:17.850
being an experimental subject.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:18.870
But this is important.

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:24.410
And that gets to the second thing we can do
to minimize the anti-tax movement, and that

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:29.930
is to people it's been shown will be more
amenable to being vaccinated as someone that

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:33.030
they knew was vaccinated and if it went well.

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:37.150
And so the more that we get into those populations,
the better it should turn out.

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:45.020
The one of the concerns I have and I'm wondering
whether you share it, is that there are many

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:51.470
articles that, from my perspective, are underselling
the benefits of in particular the two vaccines

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:52.830
that are approved right now.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:59.400
And sometimes you will see maybe not headlines,
but like some headlines that will say even

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:03.090
when vaccinated, nobody can do anything differently.

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:05.870
Everything has to remain the same for a very
long time.

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:10.889
And when you sometimes get into the details
or look at the blogs of immunologists as an

00:06:10.889 --> 00:06:15.750
example, you will actually see much more interesting
information like, listen, there is going to

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:22.520
be some risk no matter what, but a small group
of vaccinated adults, 10 days pass dose number

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:26.470
two is at very low risk to do an indoor gathering.

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:30.660
In particular, if everybody works from home,
you know, more sort of like meat on the bone

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:32.900
about there really are some differences.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:36.660
And this is a game changer and it will be
more of one as more people get vaccinated.

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:40.740
Do you think my concern is warranted about
the underselling of the vaccines?

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:45.661
It is, although, again, we don't want to come
across as selling a used car, right, but I

00:06:45.661 --> 00:06:49.300
think you look at these vaccines are truly
miraculous.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:55.300
The magnitude of efficacy and frankly, safety
as well is far beyond what any of us thought

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:58.490
a year ago we would be able to achieve, especially
within this time frame.

00:06:58.490 --> 00:07:01.330
And I would say it's better than the Apollo
mission.

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:04.091
That being said, we are underselling it.

00:07:04.091 --> 00:07:08.639
And I think that the proper way to address
this, what you just mentioned, which is very

00:07:08.639 --> 00:07:15.240
valid, is to say, look, we don't yet know
after you're vaccinated whether you might

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:18.050
be able to communicate virus to others.

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:19.460
And we want to communicate to people.

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:25.081
The last thing that you want to do is to unintentionally
infect your grandparents, your children, your

00:07:25.081 --> 00:07:26.430
grandchildren.

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:31.200
And so just to be safe, let's keep up those
safety measures until we have established

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.440
herd immunity.

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:34.770
And let's be clear what herd immunity really
means.

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:39.720
And I think most reasonable people will say,
oh, if I'm protecting my neighbors by doing

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:42.090
this, that's a great reason to do it.

00:07:42.090 --> 00:07:44.840
Not that it's this onerous thing that we have
to continue to do.

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:49.520
You were talking about the Republican pushback
to vaccination.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:55.090
This is simply a continuation of the denial
that the pandemic was real, the denial that

00:07:55.090 --> 00:08:01.250
the masks are effective and we have to get
past that and say, look, independent of what

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:02.250
your political views are.

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:04.680
Here's what the science tells us.

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:13.030
What is the best way for someone to accurately
sort of pass as you talk about so many rumors

00:08:13.030 --> 00:08:16.810
every single day, there's something the medicine,
a vaccine doesn't work against the South African

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:17.810
variant.

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:18.810
Oh, it does.

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:23.680
But it just is more borderline in terms of
the immunity versus being more robust against

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:24.750
the UK variant.

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:27.290
And maybe that's not true.

00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:30.790
We need to get to one level of herd immunity
versus another.

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:35.150
And then the next day we find out the number
is actually different for the average person,

00:08:35.150 --> 00:08:38.700
particularly people not like me who do this
for a living, but people who have other jobs

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:42.650
where they can't follow this stuff necessarily
that that closely.

00:08:42.650 --> 00:08:48.270
What's the best way to stay up on the sort
of top line realities are about cases, about

00:08:48.270 --> 00:08:50.970
deaths, about vaccination treatment, et cetera.

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:57.050
Well, now that the Centers for Disease Control
and Prevention is under capable hands, again,

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:59.500
I think that you can go back to trusting them.

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:06.330
Frankly, we had the best public health group
on the planet until this pandemic broke out

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:07.960
and they lost a lot of their credibility.

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:11.300
And I, frankly, was telling people, don't
listen to CDC because they weren't giving

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:12.480
the right information.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:17.730
But I would say if you had one go to reliable
place, it would be the CDC.

00:09:17.730 --> 00:09:23.140
Otherwise, don't Google go, for example, to
Mayo Clinic or go to whatever your local hospital

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:24.150
has to say.

00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:27.920
Look what they have to say, Google and Twitter.

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:32.361
I mean, one of the amazing things is that
if you look at the antibiotics movement, not

00:09:32.361 --> 00:09:39.520
just for this pandemic, but MMR and other
vaccines, it is just comforting to know that

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:45.690
about 85 to 90 percent of the tweets that
are anti vax are coming from Russian troll

00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:51.130
farms and all they are doing is really undermining
and their intent is to undermine belief in

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:52.700
authorities.

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:57.470
And so I have not naive belief in authorities,
but especially the CDC.

00:09:57.470 --> 00:10:01.540
It's turned itself around just in the past
few weeks, still got a lot of room to make

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:07.700
up, but go to the major universities, other
places that are not making money or profiting

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:09.820
in any way from this.

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:12.760
For the most part, the pharma companies have
actually been surprisingly transparent.

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:13.930
There have been some exceptions.

00:10:13.930 --> 00:10:16.190
And I've been a big critic of the exceptions.

00:10:16.190 --> 00:10:18.790
And we need to be critics of the exceptions.

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:23.740
And but I would say that most people so far
have come together and been mostly responsible

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:26.480
when it comes to vaccines per day.

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:31.000
When Joe Biden was just days from being sworn
in, he was talking about a million a day for

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.000
100 days.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:36.910
Of course, at the time, the approved vaccines
are are two doses, meaning you're talking

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:41.730
about vaccinating 50 million people were now
hopefully getting closer to the approval of

00:10:41.730 --> 00:10:45.310
the JMJ vaccine, which will be a one dose.

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:50.029
And then there's potentially more more vaccines
coming when when you're looking at this.

00:10:50.029 --> 00:10:56.089
I mean, it seems to me that with a third vaccine,
two and a half to three million doses a day,

00:10:56.089 --> 00:10:59.970
total is is reasonable, which seems like it
would be a major accomplishment.

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:04.570
But we're still talking about months there
in the best of cases until everybody can get

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:05.570
vaccinated.

00:11:05.570 --> 00:11:07.740
What sort of numbers are you looking at?

00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:12.880
I mean, I think the two key numbers to remember
are three hundred and fifty million Americans.

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:13.880
Right.

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:18.471
Which if we forget the JMJ vaccine for a minute,
that means seven hundred million doses, which

00:11:18.471 --> 00:11:19.471
is a lot.

00:11:19.471 --> 00:11:21.240
And this is a brand new technology.

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:26.450
But then the other number is seven and a half
billion humans, which then means 15 billion

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:27.450
doses.

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:29.890
And again, this isn't over until it's completely
over.

00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:36.200
Now, I believe and hope that the JMJ vaccine
is likely to be approved based on what we've

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:37.200
seen.

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:39.070
Its efficacy numbers are, again, very impressive.

00:11:39.070 --> 00:11:43.640
They're not quite up to the Marnay vaccine
numbers, but at least it could get someone

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:47.430
some transient protection, if you will.

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:50.950
And future studies can determine, well, maybe
someone who got one vaccine will need a boost

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:52.100
of another.

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:57.030
But I the most remarkable thing about the
vaccine numbers is not necessarily just the

00:11:57.030 --> 00:12:01.400
magnitude of efficacy, which is exceeding
at this point ninety five percent.

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:05.080
And based on the Israeli study, it may be
closer to ninety nine point five percent.

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:06.080
Right.

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:11.871
But it's the fact that the disease severity
is greatly reduced and people, frankly, are

00:12:11.871 --> 00:12:13.990
not dying or getting severe disease.

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:15.510
And that's where we want to be.

00:12:15.510 --> 00:12:19.970
If you're stuck with feeling bad for a few
days or getting a cold, which most of coronaviruses

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:25.081
cause a cold, that's infinitely better than
having to be intubated and, Lord forbid, pass

00:12:25.081 --> 00:12:26.780
away or have your relatives do.

00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:30.990
So, I would say the big numbers now are we've
got to ramp up production.

00:12:30.990 --> 00:12:33.720
The need now, the concern now is not anti
vax.

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:38.590
The concern is manufacturing and making sure
that the manufacturing quality still stays

00:12:38.590 --> 00:12:39.590
high.

00:12:39.590 --> 00:12:43.850
And that's where, again, FDA has been very
consistent and fantastic about doing that.

00:12:43.850 --> 00:12:51.680
There have been some some preference based
in some cases almost on accidental circumstances

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:56.510
that have surfaced, which suggests then again,
I want to be careful to make clear that we're

00:12:56.510 --> 00:13:01.300
talking about something we're still learning
about, which suggests that in some cases,

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:05.600
if at the time that the second dose would
be given, you just kept waiting, you would

00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:12.440
get a very close level of protection to what
you get from the second dose plus seven to

00:13:12.440 --> 00:13:13.610
14 days.

00:13:13.610 --> 00:13:18.440
Is that an interesting path that you think
needs to be looked at in terms of possibly

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:22.680
being able to expand the number of people
inoculated with the vaccines were expecting

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:23.810
to have?

00:13:23.810 --> 00:13:30.110
If the data show it, I think that we run a
risk, there was there was discussion about

00:13:30.110 --> 00:13:31.860
giving everybody one shot.

00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:32.860
Right.

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:37.430
And even if it falls outside the window that
was done in the clinical trials, giving them

00:13:37.430 --> 00:13:42.031
a later shot, we just frankly don't have the
data to say whether that's useful or not.

00:13:42.031 --> 00:13:46.529
And the situation we don't want to end up
in is that we give everyone one shot and one

00:13:46.529 --> 00:13:51.490
shot turns out to be insufficient and we have
to start and turn around and begin afresh.

00:13:51.490 --> 00:13:55.950
Right now, everyone needs two shots, even
if you already had one and we just don't that

00:13:55.950 --> 00:13:58.540
we have to be guided by the data.

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:02.340
We the last administration was frustrating
because they didn't seem to want to track

00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:03.340
any data.

00:14:03.340 --> 00:14:06.470
And this administration, I think, is open
to it.

00:14:06.470 --> 00:14:09.510
There's going to be pressure to hit these
artificial numbers.

00:14:09.510 --> 00:14:12.700
I would say 100 million and one hundred days
is great.

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:15.880
All I care about is as many as can be safely
done.

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:17.760
That's the number we need to get.

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:21.050
And hopefully that will be well in excess
of one hundred million, no doubt about it.

00:14:21.050 --> 00:14:22.050
Yeah.

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:24.320
And two million last Saturday and two million
last Sunday.

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:28.390
Certainly our great, great, great numbers
to start seeing.

00:14:28.390 --> 00:14:34.380
We've been speaking with Michael Kench, author
of Between Hope and Fear A History of Vaccines,

00:14:34.380 --> 00:14:38.480
also associate vice chancellor at Washington
University in St. Louis.

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:39.600
Such a pleasure having you on.

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:42.610
I really appreciate your time.

